# 3 readings by claude-opus-5-5, compared
aquinas-st-i-ii-2.md:1: argue/readings: S5 is read 2 ways: aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2 has nothing from it; aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.2 and aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.3 have "overflow → more_passion"; they differ when only "the joy overflows into the sensitive appetite" is true, which the first allows
aquinas-st-i-ii-2.md:1: argue/answered: S5: answered no, which keeps aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.2 and aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.3, to: Suppose "the joy overflows into the sensitive appetite" is true and "the more perfect the virtue is, the more it causes passion" is false. Is S5, "Wherefore by reason of this kind of overflow, the more perfect a virtue is, the more does it cause passion.", true then?
aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2: argue/readings: what the text leaves unstated is read 2 ways: aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2 has "overflow → more_passion"; aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.2 and aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.3 have "perfected"; they differ when only "the joy overflows into the sensitive appetite" and "the more perfect the virtue is, the more it causes passion" are true, which the first allows
aquinas-st-i-ii-2.md:1: argue/readings: the conclusion is read 2 ways: aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2 has "perfected → more_passion"; aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.2 and aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.3 have "more_passion"; they differ when nothing is true, which the first allows
aquinas-st-i-ii-2.md:1: argue/answered: the conclusion: answered no, which keeps aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.2 and aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.3, to: Suppose "the joy is increased through the perfection of justice" and "the more perfect the virtue is, the more it causes passion" are false. Is the conclusion, "Wherefore by reason of this kind of overflow, the more perfect a virtue is, the more does it cause passion.", true then?
aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2: argue/readings: U1: aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.2 and aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.3 take for granted "the joy is increased through the perfection of justice"; aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2 does not
aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2: argue/answered: U1: answered yes, which keeps aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.2 and aquinas-st-i-ii-2.logic.r2.3, to: Does the text's argument take this for granted, whether or not it says so: "the joy is increased through the perfection of justice"? Answer yes if the author would accept it as part of the argument.
